{
  "units": "meters",
  "floor": 14,
  "source": "Traced from the recovered original Northeastern University Vancouver 14th Floor plan image (world/data/source/floor-14-plan.png), pasted into chat 2026-07-26, recovered from an old chat transcript 2026-08-02. Replaces an earlier eyeballed axis-aligned approximation. Coordinates are hand-traced off the raster image, not survey-accurate.",
  "note": "Traced from the recovered original 14th-floor plan image (world/data/source/floor-14-plan.png, 753x436, whitespace-trimmed to 473x364). Transform: world_x = px * 0.01522, world_z = (1820 - py) * 0.01522, where (px,py) are pixel coords on a 5x-upscaled 2365x1820 copy of the trimmed plan (so 0.01522 m per 5x-pixel = 0.0761 m per original pixel). Image y grows downward (south); world z grows upward on the page (north), hence the (1820-py) flip. Footprint ends up ~36m x 27.7m, matching the plan's true ~1.30 aspect ratio (vs. the old file's 1.71). Coordinates are hand-traced off the raster image, not a survey -- good for a browser-demo navmesh, not construction. Rooms are rotated polygons (parallelograms/wedges/trapezoids) matching the plan's pinwheel layout, not axis-aligned boxes. Kitchen's curved west edge, 1430's and 1409's curved edges, and the Event Space 'island table' are approximated as short straight polylines/omitted (island table is furniture, not a wall). The building core is TWO separate axis-aligned horizontal bands (upper: locker + stairs + 4 elevator shafts; lower: 4 more shafts), matching the source, with the three washrooms as enclosed rooms along the lower band's south edge. South and North Collaboration Space are open-plan (no enclosing walls), per the source. Entrance is placed just east of the elevator core, in the open pocket between the core and Kitchen/Event Space -- the real elevator lobby is the walkway around the core; this is the most defensible single point since the core itself is a hole.",
